        ("How do I withdraw from a course?", "Submit a course withdrawal form through the registrar's office or student portal before the withdrawal deadline. Withdrawals after the add/drop period may result in a 'W' on your transcript. Consult your advisor before withdrawing to understand the impact on financial aid and progress.", "registration"),
        ("What is the maximum course load per semester?", "Full-time students may take up to 18 credit hours per semester without special permission. Overloads up to 21 hours require dean approval. Part-time students may take up to 11 credit hours. Check your program requirements for recommended course loads.", "registration"),
        ("How do I join a student club or organization?", "Browse available clubs on the student activities portal. Attend the club fair at the beginning of each semester or contact the club directly. Some clubs require an application or auditions. Membership is free for most organizations.", "student-life"),
        ("Where can I get help with writing assignments?", "The writing center offers free one-on-one tutoring for essays, research papers, and presentations. Drop in during operating hours or schedule an appointment online. They can help with structure, citations, and grammar at any stage of the writing process.", "academics"),
        ("What career services are available?", "The career center provides resume reviews, mock interviews, job boards, and career counseling. They also host employer recruitment events and graduate school fairs. All services are free for current students and recent graduates.", "career"),
